From: pepp <pepp@users.noreply.gitlab.freedesktop.org>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: keep GFX12 DCC blits off the SDMA move entity
Message-ID: <gitlab-drm/amd-5663-note-3664147>

Force move entity 0 for AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_GFX12_DCC buffers being moved
into VRAM from non-VRAM, so a DCC blit is never handed to the alternate
SDMA engine. On Navi 4x that produces artifacts after S3 suspend/resume.

Reconstructed: the diff in the issue note is space-indented where the
tree uses tabs and its last three context lines are truncated, so the
hunk body was rebuilt from the tree. The added lines are the author's,
content-identical modulo leading whitespace.

Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/amd/-/work_items/5663#note_3664147
Reported-by: pepp <pepp@users.noreply.gitlab.freedesktop.org>
Signed-off-by: Sleepy <sleepy@localhost>
Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -415,6 +415,11 @@ static int amdgpu_move_blit(struct ttm_buffer_object *bo,
 
 	e = atomic_inc_return(&adev->mman.next_move_entity) %
 			      adev->mman.num_move_entities;
+	bool to_vram = new_mem && new_mem->mem_type == TTM_PL_VRAM;
+	bool not_from_vram = !old_mem || old_mem->mem_type != TTM_PL_VRAM;
+	if (to_vram && not_from_vram && abo->flags & AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_GFX12_DCC)
+		e = 0;
+
 	entity = &adev->mman.move_entities[e];
 
 	r = amdgpu_ttm_copy_mem_to_mem(adev,
